          <div id="playerManagerPanel" class="accordion-collapse collapse">
            <div class="accordion-body">
              <p>
                Throughout my career as a Software Engineer, I have designed and implemented multiple solutions that enable seamless communication between distributed systems.
                One of the most notable projects was my work on the <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@@jobboss4393/search?query=Lojic" target="_blank">Lojic Dashboards</a>
                platform and its integration with enterprise ERP software.
              </p>

              <p>
                <div class="container text-center">
                  <div class="row">
                    <!-- Image 1 -->
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                      <img src="images/lojic_dashboards.png" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-sm" alt="Lojic Dashboards"
                           @onclick='@(() => OnImageClick("Lojic Dashboards", "lojic_dashboards.png"))' style="cursor: pointer;">
                    </div>

                    <!-- Image 2 -->
                    <div class="col-md-6">
                      <img src="images/lojic_dashboards_display.png" class="img-fluid rounded shadow-sm" alt="Lojic Dashboards Display"
                           @onclick='@(() => OnImageClick("Lojic Dashboards - Display on Shop Floor", "lojic_dashboards_display.png"))' style="cursor: pointer;">
                    </div>
                  </div>
                </div>
              </p>

              <p>
                In this role, I developed and maintained services that facilitated data exchange between the dashboard platform
                and various ERP systems, ensuring <strong>scalability, reliability, and security</strong>. This involved:
              </p>
              <ul>
                <li>Designing <strong>RESTful APIs</strong> for data integration.</li>
                <li>Handling <strong>real-time data streaming</strong> and <strong>asynchronous processing</strong> using cloud services.</li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                Additionally, I created the Player software, a cross-platform application deployed on
                Windows and Linux devices, typically installed on <strong>single-board computers</strong> for digital signage purposes.
                The management layer of this system was hosted in Azure, where I designed a cloud-based command and control system.
                <div class="my-4 container text-center">
                  <figure>
                    <figcaption class="mt-2 text-muted">A command and control system for managing devices on the shop floor, primarily used to display real-time dashboards.</figcaption>
                    <img src="images/player_manager.png" class="img-fluid w-75 d-block mx-auto rounded shadow-lg" alt="Player Manager"
                         @onclick='@(() => OnImageClick("Player Manager", "player_manager.png"))' style="cursor: pointer;">
                  </figure>
                </div>
              </p>

              This architecture leveraged:
              <ul>
                <li><strong>Azure Queues & Blob Storage</strong> for asynchronous messaging and configuration management.</li>
                <li><strong>Microservices</strong> to handle command processing, player status monitoring, and remote updates.</li>
                <li><strong>Secure API endpoints</strong> for managing device communication and remote control functions.</li>
              </ul>

              <p>
                This system allowed administrators to remotely configure players, send commands (e.g., reboots, content updates),
                and retrieve device status through a web-based management portal.
              </p>

              <p>
                My experience with <strong>SOA</strong> extends beyond this project, as I have also worked on cloud-native applications using
                <strong>Azure Function Apps, Durable Functions,</strong> and <strong>microservices architectures</strong> to build scalable and
                resilient enterprise solutions.
              </p>

              <p>
                By leveraging <strong>SOA principles</strong>, I have successfully designed systems that promote
                <strong>modularity, interoperability, and maintainability </strong>,
                ensuring smooth integration between various business applications and cloud services.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
